+# myrmidon(G1): ``reflect`` synthesizes the answer with an LLM over the whole bank, so it
+# is far slower than recall/retain: a busy bank can take several minutes to answer, well
+# past the shared client timeout above, which then aborts the call while the bank is
+# still working and answers correctly. Own ceiling, overridable per profile via
+# ``reflect_timeout`` / HINDSIGHT_REFLECT_TIMEOUT. Deliberately set above the bank's own
+# reflect wall-clock limit (which answers its own timeout error before this elapses) so
+# the client waits for the bank's own verdict instead of abandoning a live request one
+# second before it lands.
+_DEFAULT_REFLECT_TIMEOUT = 360  # seconds
